        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The doctor elicited/used the real-world barriers of unreadable sheets, injection fear, and unclear follow-up, then created concrete fallbacks involving nurse verification, ED/clinic review, record keeping, and original-team review. This had meaningful impact by moving the patient from unsafe home guessing to verified instructions and follow-up.",
